# PostgreSQL Rules

## Types
| Use case | Correct | Avoid |
|---|---|---|
| IDs | `bigint` / `uuid` | `int` |
| Strings | `text` | `varchar(n)` |
| Email identity | `citext` or normalized lower-case `text` + unique index | case-sensitive raw `text` |
| Timestamps | `timestamptz` | `timestamp` |
| Money | `numeric(12,2)` | `float` |
| JSON | `jsonb` | `json` |
| Embeddings | `vector(n)` + model/version metadata | raw vector without dimensions |

## Schema design
- Every table has a primary key; prefer `bigint generated always as identity`
  for internal records and `uuid default gen_random_uuid()` for public or
  distributed IDs.
- Tables are plural `snake_case`; columns are singular `snake_case`.
- User-mutable tables include `created_at`, `updated_at`, and `created_by` when
  actor attribution matters. Soft-delete tables use `deleted_at timestamptz`,
  not only `is_deleted boolean`.
- Foreign keys declare explicit `ON DELETE` behavior (`restrict`, `cascade`, or
  `set null`) based on product ownership semantics.
- Multi-tenant Supabase SaaS defaults to shared tables with `tenant_id` + RLS;
  document any schema-per-tenant/project-per-tenant deviation.
- Identify PII columns and restrict sensitive fields with column-level grants
  when row-level access is broader than field-level access.

## Indexes
- B-tree default. Composite `(a, b)` equality-first.
- `GIN` for `jsonb @>` and full-text. `BRIN` for time-series ranges.
- Partial: `WHERE deleted_at IS NULL`. Covering: `INCLUDE (...)`.
- Index every hot `WHERE`, `JOIN`, `ORDER BY`, foreign key, and pagination
  cursor column.
- Index every non-PK column referenced in RLS policies, especially `user_id` and
  `tenant_id`.

## Queries
- Parameterised only — no string interpolation.
- Hot queries must show index usage in `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` (no `Seq Scan` on big tables).
- No `SELECT *` in services.
- No N+1 loops — batch related reads with `IN (...)`, joins, or preloaded repository methods.
- Large reads must be bounded with `LIMIT`, cursor pagination, or a documented hard cap.
- Realtime subscriptions include filters; no broad table subscriptions for
  multi-tenant/user data.
- Full-text search uses Postgres `tsvector` + GIN before external search for
  ordinary app search.
- JSONB is for sparse/variable attributes only; queried JSONB has a GIN or
  expression index.
- Vector search chooses HNSW vs IVFFlat intentionally, stores model/version, and
  benchmarks recall/performance before production.

## Migrations
- One concern per migration; reversible where feasible.
- Non-null on big table: nullable → backfill in batches → NOT NULL.
- Drops are two-phase (stop reading → deploy → drop).
- Production rollback is forward-only: write an undo migration instead of
  editing applied migrations or restoring from backup. Never write `DROP TABLE`
  without a tested rollback/undo plan.
- Add foreign keys on large tables with `NOT VALID`, then `VALIDATE CONSTRAINT`.
- Avoid one-shot `ALTER COLUMN TYPE` and large-table `NOT NULL DEFAULT`; use
  expand-contract migrations.

## RLS (multi-tenant)
- ON for every user-data table. Default-deny. Per-role per-action policies. Test with anon + authed in CI.
- Policies are operation-specific for `SELECT` / `INSERT` / `UPDATE` / `DELETE`.
  Write policies include `WITH CHECK` as well as `USING` where applicable.
- Policies target `TO authenticated` or the intended role explicitly; avoid
  accidental default `public`.
- Wrap stable Supabase helpers as `(select auth.uid())` / `(select auth.jwt())`
  in policies when possible.

## Connections
- Use a pooler (PgBouncer / Supavisor) for serverless / high concurrency.
- Transaction-mode pooling breaks prepared statements — match driver config.

## Operations gates
- Supabase Security Advisor and Performance Advisor findings are clean or
  documented before production release.
- Enable `pg_stat_statements` on Supabase/Postgres before production
  observability is marked ready. Surface slow queries by normalized query,
  p95/mean execution time, calls, and rows read when available, then include a
  concrete index suggestion or an `EXPLAIN ANALYZE` follow-up. Never paste bind
  values or PII into reports.
- Backups have a tested restore path. Free-tier Supabase projects need explicit
  export/off-site backup planning before production data lands.
